    "pressure": {
      "file": "universal_joint_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Joint angle β makes the output speed fluctuate",
      "description": "A single Cardan joint transmits rotation through an angle, but not at constant speed: the output angular velocity swings between ω·cos β and ω/cos β twice every revolution (for β = 25° about −9 % to +10 %). Two joints with the yokes of the intermediate shaft in phase and equal angles (Z or W arrangement) cancel the fluctuation. The needle bearings in the cross only oscillate, so they need a minimum working angle (≈ 1–2°) to spread grease and avoid brinelling.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
  },
